/-!
# Checked reductions for the alternating-seven endpoint of 11.4.2

The original moving fixed seed excludes the four-dimensional section using
the earlier PSL2(4) quotient marking; five-divisibility of the actual
L1 image is proved through its solvable action kernel. The actual ratio bound
implies equality of the two-ranks of R1 and T. Finally the literal field
action is incompatible with innerness on the same seed image.

This module does not assert the source contradiction. Natural six-space
recognition, the transposition and ratio-one rows, the maximum elementary
field witness, and Thompson control from the original natural L-module
must still be constructed and connected by the final assembly owner.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.4.2, printed p.777.
-/
